{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqh0gwz1mxc","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"OVERRIDE: probe-runner keep uses createEdge not keepEdge — keepEdge no-ops on sub-0.55 autowire sessions","summary":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: spike note-mqgwr63ms7q documents the our-way keep step as keepEdge, but keepEdge (lib/judge.js:580) ONLY promotes a PRE-EXISTING weight-0 autowire candidate edge (e.judged===false) to its cosine. If a kept session's autowire cosine fell below SEMANTIC_AUTOWIRE_THRESHOLD (0.55, daemon.js:1419), NO candidate edge was ever seeded, so keepEdge returns false / no-ops and that session never surfaces in GET /task/context. Reproduced live on bench fixture multi-hop q2 (gold ciabatta): the blind judge correctly kept session 2, but keepEdge produced an empty dependencySummaries and our-way answered \"I don't know\". FIX (bench/agent-memory/probe_runner.py run_our_way): assert the kept edges via createEdge verdict ({createEdge:{from:note,to:probe,weight:0.5}}) instead. createEdge (routes/judge.js:156) calls overlayStore.addEdge('context',weight) which UPSERTS (lib/overlay.js:409) — promotes an existing candidate AND creates a missing one, judged:true — so a kept session is always retrieval-visible regardless of its autowire score. This changes only the edge-assert primitive; the blind judge still owns which sessions are kept (honesty bar intact). The spike's keepEdge worked only because it tested a single strong candidate that autowire reliably seeded.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T19:04:25.069Z","vec":[-0.1258925199508667,0.022354092448949814,-0.02772444859147072,0.08988305181264877,0.07693939656019211,-0.022883109748363495,0.06374379992485046,-0.03476845473051071,-0.019269390031695366,0.020099833607673645,-0.0120548689737916,-0.05080121383070946,0.003751450916752219,0.03326214849948883,-0.030176201835274696,0.04674174636602402,0.086812324821949,-0.07077117264270782,-0.029898306354880333,-0.035693079233169556,0.055469609797000885,-0.00126409542281